        ns1:SourceField ;
    rdfs:label "Indirect support"@en ;
    dcterms:source <file:///D:/Work-Documents/13_Research/2026_Research/FAIR/research-repos/FAIR-DAMA-FAIRMM/sources/2026-11-16/DAMA_Segments_High_Level_v1.18.0.md#L751> ;
    ns1:fieldHeading "Indirect support" ;
    ns1:sourcePosition 10 ;
    ns1:sourceText "Indirect support: Architecture ownership and review can align implemented resources with agreed FAIR representations and service requirements." .

ns1:ACT-02-002-field-11 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        ns1:SourceField ;
    rdfs:label "What would demonstrate the supported FAIR requirement"@en ;
    dcterms:source <file:///D:/Work-Documents/13_Research/2026_Research/FAIR/research-repos/FAIR-DAMA-FAIRMM/sources/2026-11-16/DAMA_Segments_High_Level_v1.18.0.md#L751> ;
    ns1:fieldHeading "What would demonstrate the supported FAIR requirement" ;
    ns1:sourcePosition 11 ;
    ns1:sourceText "I1: Inspect the implemented language, shared specification and sample data/metadata representations. Parse them independently and verify that the language is formal, accessible, shared and broadly applicable; schema syntax or diagrams alone are insufficient.; I2: Inspect the vocabulary term identifiers and versions actually used in data/metadata; assess the vocabulary itself for FAIR identifiers, discovery, access, representation, licensing and provenance. An internal glossary or taxonomy alone is insufficient.; I3: Inspect sample data/metadata for references to identifiable related resources with explicit relation types and context; check targets and meanings. Matching keys or diagrammed entity relationships alone are insufficient.; Supporting-process evidence: inspect the named deliverable and its approval/maintenance records separately from the resource tests." .

