    ns1:fieldHeading "How they can support FAIR" ;
    ns1:sourcePosition 9 ;
    ns1:sourceText "No direct FAIR requirement is established by this ethical-practice activity or its named deliverables. Ethical responsibility and FAIR fulfilment are related but distinct." .

ns1:ACT-14-004-field-1 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        ns1:SourceField ;
    rdfs:label "Activities"@en ;
    dcterms:source <file:///D:/Work-Documents/13_Research/2026_Research/FAIR/research-repos/FAIR-DAMA-FAIRMM/sources/2026-11-16/DAMA_Segments_High_Level_v1.18.0.md#L2285> ;
    ns1:fieldHeading "Activities" ;
    ns1:sourcePosition 1 ;
    ns1:sourceText "Identify and Remediate Gaps in Existing Practices" .

ns1:ACT-14-004-field-10 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        ns1:SourceField ;
    rdfs:label "Indirect support"@en ;
    dcterms:source <file:///D:/Work-Documents/13_Research/2026_Research/FAIR/research-repos/FAIR-DAMA-FAIRMM/sources/2026-11-16/DAMA_Segments_High_Level_v1.18.0.md#L2285> ;
    ns1:fieldHeading "Indirect support" ;
    ns1:sourcePosition 10 ;
    ns1:sourceText "Remediation can address gaps in access controls and reuse permissions only where those gaps and the affected resources are identified." .

ns1:ACT-14-004-field-11 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        ns1:SourceField ;
    rdfs:label "What would demonstrate the supported FAIR requirement"@en ;
    dcterms:source <file:///D:/Work-Documents/13_Research/2026_Research/FAIR/research-repos/FAIR-DAMA-FAIRMM/sources/2026-11-16/DAMA_Segments_High_Level_v1.18.0.md#L2285> ;
    ns1:fieldHeading "What would demonstrate the supported FAIR requirement" ;
    ns1:sourcePosition 11 ;
    ns1:sourceText "Inspect approved policy or control requirements that explicitly distinguish access authorization from permitted reuse. Test any resulting authentication and authorization procedure for identified resources (A1.2) and inspect the clear, accessible usage licence attached to data and metadata (R1.1). An ethics statement, privacy notice or generic compliance metric alone is insufficient." .

